      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{63691297469f06772579fe6f|full_name} Unfortunately it seems kinda random, but it's almost always missing these days, so it shouldn't be hard to catch. I have my SDK window up all the time as a tab behind the inspector. Pretty much every time that I switch back the the SDK from the inspector the validations are missing again. I can reliably get them to come back if the unity editor window loses focus and then I click back, or if I do a build and the build finishes. \n\nIt seems to be more than just visually missing too, I've had it start building and then fail somewhere with one of the validations that would normally stop you from pressing the build button like streaming mipmaps or wherever.",
